# WildfireGuardian Route-Check API: runtime settings (all optional).
# The API uses no API keys, tokens or other secrets, and makes no network calls at runtime.
# Copy this file to api/.env (git-ignored). The make targets (make api, make api-test, ...) load plain
# WFG_API_NAME=value lines from it; a variable already set in your shell wins. Without make:
#   set -a; . api/.env; set +a
# Experiment constants (30 s budget, 3072 MiB guard, 300 m snap, 10 kW/m2, 100 kJ/m2, 120 s) are fixed in api/config.py.

# Root of the recorded inputs (graphs/, latest_inputs_try02/). Default: <repo>/data/routing
# WFG_API_DATA_ROOT=data/routing

# Job folders, the ablation kit copy and per-request packets. Default: <repo>/artifacts/api_runtime (git-ignored)
# WFG_API_RUNTIME_DIR=artifacts/api_runtime

# Concurrent route checks (spawn process pool). Default: physical cores - 2 (minimum 1)
# WFG_API_WORKERS=4

# Bind address and port. Defaults: 127.0.0.1 and 8765
# WFG_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# WFG_API_PORT=8765

# Interpreter that launches kit workers and child processes. Default: the server's sys.executable
# WFG_API_PYTHON=.venv/bin/python

# Fallback git commit for provenance, used only when the checkout has no git metadata (git rev-parse HEAD wins).
# WFG_API_GIT_COMMIT=
